+# Channel Links and Universal Sorting 0003 Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Release 0003 with private-channel invite links and persistent typed sorting in every table.
+
+**Architecture:** Add pure channel-link and table-sort helpers under `tam_core`, then integrate them into the main Tk UI, batch uploader and X planner. Channel link refresh reuses connections per account and stores only real links in state; sorting uses one reusable controller with persistence callbacks.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Python 3, tkinter/ttk, SQLite, Telethon 1.44.0, unittest, GitHub Actions.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-01-channel-links-and-universal-sorting-0003-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+- Base release is exactly `0002`; visible release version is `0003`.
+- No new Telegram write calls during ordinary channel inventory solely to manufacture links.
+- Explicit `Обновить ссылки` may create an invite only for an owner/admin with invite capability.
+- Preserve all 0002 persistence and upload behavior.
+- Tests are written and observed failing before production implementation.
+
